completed_at: "2026-09-08T08:53:57.316Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: "All-skipped npm, mixed checked/skipped, failed and not-checked managed sources report partial update coverage; successful checks and expected builtins retain valid semantics; SDK CLI and isolated installed-package acceptance agree."
goal: project management = context management
objective: Make package freshness claims depend on completed upstream checks
value: Agents can distinguish healthy activation from unknown update status
impact: Prevents false full-coverage receipts after npm or local adoption
parent: pm-ugqx
risk: medium
confidence: high
resolution: "Implemented honest package update coverage for skipped, failed and not-checked sources; only checked sources contribute known updates, with source-specific remediation and host-owned builtin exemptions."
expected_result: "Activation health stays distinct from upstream freshness; adopted local or npm sources remain partial until an applicable check succeeds, and strict doctor exposes that gap."
actual_result: "All 8579 tests passed at exact 100/100/100/100. Dedicated skipped/failed/mixed/unchecked controls, 137 lifecycle regressions, and strict inert-service integration passed, including both linked doctor commands. Installed npm and Bun archive packages activated successfully while reporting partial update coverage. Docstring coverage is 100 percent; all static gate components passed. Hosted review and merge verification follow this reviewed closure."
